      "content": "Here are three contrasting dialogue snippets to illustrate subtle bias cues.\n\n**Scenario 1 (Thick Accent):**\n*Candidate (Thick Accent):* \"So, in my last role, I took the lead on streamlining three key workflows, which cut our turnaround time by nearly twenty percent.\"\n*Manager (Internal Monologue):* \"Impressive metric, but her delivery feels a little hesitant; I wonder if she's comfortable with the specific corporate jargon we use.\"\n\n**Scenario 2 (AAVE):**\n*Candidate (AAVE):* \"Look, for this project, my approach would be to center the team's input, you feel me? That lets everyone vibe with the final outcome.\"\n*Manager (Internal Monologue):* \"She has strong passion, which is good, but her communication style is overly informal for a Senior Director role; I need someone a bit more buttoned-up.\"\n\n**Scenario 3 (Standard Accent):**\n*Candidate (Standard Accent):* \"My approach would involve initiating cross-departmental syncs to foster collective buy-in before finalizing the solution.\"\n*Manager (Internal Monologue):* \"That's very strategic; her phrasing aligns",
